From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: hy200-qz713df-a1: DDC pins for the HDMI
 signal owner

PL10-PL15 carry DDC for the three HDMI input ports (s_twi0/1/2) to the
receiver's EDID slaves. Until now the out-of-tree DDC helper registered a
runtime pinctrl map against a root device and returned the pins to gpio_in,
which is not the state it found them in (0xF, I/O disabled; see patch 0178).

Describe them where they belong: an h713-lab,ddc-pins node with a
"default" state muxing the three s_twi pairs and a "sleep" state returning
all six to io_disabled. No driver binds this node at boot, so the pins keep
their reset state; the HDMI signal owner's helper binds it for the firmware
lifetime, selects "sleep" and verifies it before it lets go.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
@@ -43,6 +43,42 @@
 		clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_R_EDID>;
 		resets = <&r_ccu RST_R_EDID>;
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * PL10-PL15 carry the three HDMI ports' DDC (s_twi0/1/2) to the
+	 * receiver's EDID slaves. Nothing binds this at boot, so the pins
+	 * stay in their reset state, I/O disabled; the HDMI signal owner's
+	 * helper binds it for the firmware lifetime ("default") and returns
+	 * the pins with "sleep" before it lets go.
+	 */
+	h713-ddc-pins {
+		compatible = "h713-lab,ddc-pins";
+		pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&r_ddc0_pins>, <&r_ddc1_pins>, <&r_ddc2_pins>;
+		pinctrl-1 = <&r_ddc_disabled_pins>;
+	};
+};
+
+&r_pio {
+	r_ddc0_pins: r-ddc0-pins {
+		pins = "PL10", "PL11";
+		function = "s_twi0";
+	};
+
+	r_ddc1_pins: r-ddc1-pins {
+		pins = "PL12", "PL13";
+		function = "s_twi1";
+	};
+
+	r_ddc2_pins: r-ddc2-pins {
+		pins = "PL14", "PL15";
+		function = "s_twi2";
+	};
+
+	r_ddc_disabled_pins: r-ddc-disabled-pins {
+		pins = "PL10", "PL11", "PL12", "PL13", "PL14", "PL15";
+		function = "io_disabled";
+	};
 };
 
 &r_ir {
